    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (72.21) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.07) headline the Austin Waves lineup as our elite plays. **Kyle Tucker** faces a favorable matchup against Michael King (4.39 xERA), where the lack of an elite platoon disadvantage and his high base projection anchor him as our daily ceiling. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a soft matchup against Williamson (5.64 xERA). His score is buoyed by a 19% SP skill advantage and the high-leverage opportunity of hitting second, making him an essential start. **Miguel Vargas** (62.40) also merits a mention as a high-upside play; despite facing the lefty Lynch IV, his current xwOBA of .381 and the leadoff spot provide a distinct opportunity to generate volume in a category-starved offensive environment.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Brayan Rocchio** (38.00) was the clear \"near miss,\" falling just short of our 40.0 floor. While his park environment offered a 7% boost, the 17% hit to his projection from facing an elite arm like Tolle, combined with his bottom-of-the-order positioning, forced the optimizer to keep him on the pine to conserve our daily game caps. Our roster management is further complicated by the forced absence of **Gunnar Henderson**, whose game was cancelled due to a rainout. We are also monitoring the continued inactivity of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain on the IL, limiting our depth in a week where every stolen base is at a premium. \n\nStrategic risks today center on the platoon-heavy approach forced by opposing pitching matchups. Players like **Jackson Merrill** (58.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (56.66) provide marginal value, but they require careful observation. **Jackson Merrill** carries a specific situational advantage today\u2014a +2% boost from a \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor\u2014which increases his steal probability, a key metric for our team\u2019s success. We remain hopeful that the lower-scored starters like **Liam Hicks** (43.04) can avoid becoming liabilities while we wait for high-velocity performances from the heart of our order.",
